# Remote state (S3 + DynamoDB lock) — copy to backend.tf when you are ready.
# Do NOT commit real bucket/table names with secrets; names alone are fine.
#
# Why remote state?
#   Local terraform.tfstate is fine for learning on one laptop. Teams need a
#   shared, locked state so two people (or CI + you) never apply at once.
#   Kubernetes analogy: etcd is the cluster's source of truth; Terraform state
#   is yours for cloud resources.
#
# Setup (once, in the AWS console or a bootstrap script — outside this module):
#   1. Create an S3 bucket with versioning ON and block public access ON.
#   2. Create a DynamoDB table with partition key LockID (String) for locks.
#   3. Create an AWS Budgets alert at $20/month (email yourself).
#   4. Rename this file to backend.tf, fill in the names, then:
#        terraform init -reconfigure
#
# terraform {
#   backend "s3" {
#     bucket         = "YOUR-UNIQUE-TFSTATE-BUCKET"
#     key            = "grow-room-platform/dev/terraform.tfstate"
#     region         = "us-west-2"
#     dynamodb_table = "YOUR-TF-LOCK-TABLE"
#     encrypt        = true
#   }
# }
